Whisper: check for updates at Whisper's update host

What: the update URL in application.ini is
https://footprintsntrails.github.io/whisper-browser/update/1/%CHANNEL%/%BUILD_TARGET%/update.xml
instead of Mozilla's aus5.mozilla.org address.
Why: Whisper's updates are static files on GitHub Pages, one update.xml per channel
and build target (for example release/Linux_x86_64-gcc3), next to the complete MARs
in the GitHub release. Only the channel and the build target are in the address:
Firefox's own address also sends the version, build ID, locale, OS version, CPU
features and distribution, which a static host has no use for.
---
diff --git a/build/application.ini.in b/build/application.ini.in
index 6df13230a4..980d29e15d 100644
--- a/build/application.ini.in
+++ b/build/application.ini.in
@@ -52,5 +52,10 @@ ServerURL=@MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_URL@/submit?id=@MOZ_APP_ID@&version=@MOZ_APP_VERSIO
 
 #if MOZ_UPDATER
 [AppUpdate]
-URL=https://@MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST@/update/6/%PRODUCT%/%VERSION%/%BUILD_ID%/%BUILD_TARGET%/%LOCALE%/%CHANNEL%/%OS_VERSION%/%SYSTEM_CAPABILITIES%/%DISTRIBUTION%/%DISTRIBUTION_VERSION%/update.xml
+#if 0
+; Whisper: updates come from Whisper's static update host (GitHub Pages), one
+; update.xml per channel and build target; nothing else about this copy of the
+; browser is sent. gecko/scripts/update/update-xml.py writes these files.
+#endif
+URL=https://footprintsntrails.github.io/whisper-browser/update/1/%CHANNEL%/%BUILD_TARGET%/update.xml
 #endif
